  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Particularly on a touch display, I can only hit the target for dragging a noodle less than 10% of the time. The target box should probably be bigger than it is.\n\nWhen I do somehow succeed at getting a noodle, I now have to somehow repeat the feat, but now the noodle is directly under my finger, making it impossible to see where it currently is. It should probably be some distance above the cursor? Perhaps the valid drop zone could be larger as well? For instance, I tried to drag something to somewhere with only one input, so arguably the drop zone should be the entire node.",
